-- ----- fragment: minion_isaiah_57.sql (Isaiah 57) -----
-- Chapter: Isaiah 57 — THE RIGHTEOUS GATHERED / THE CONTRITE / PEACE FAR AND NEAR. The chapter opens
-- with a mercy hidden in plain sight: *The righteous perisheth, and no man layeth it to heart: and
-- merciful men are taken away, none considering that the righteous is taken away from the evil to come*
-- (57:1) — *He shall enter into peace: they shall rest in their beds* (57:2). The righteous are GATHERED
-- TO REST before the judgment falls. Between the opening lament and the closing peace stands the lawsuit
-- against the idolaters (57:3-13), but the chapter's crown is the Name itself: *thus saith the high and
-- lofty One that inhabiteth eternity, whose name is Holy; I dwell in the high and holy place, with him
-- also that is of a contrite and humble spirit* (57:15) — the transcendent-yet-near Holy One who dwells
-- with the contrite. And then the gospel of the two houses: *Peace, peace to him that is far off, and to
-- him that is near, saith Yahuah (LORD); and I will heal him* (57:19) — the scattered of both houses and
-- those near brought into ONE peace (NOT replacement, Romans 11:1-2 guard). The chapter closes with the
-- twin refrain of the wicked excluded: *There is no peace, saith my Elohim (God), to the wicked* (57:21).
-- Tag: isa57   Temp view: _s303_isa57_lookup
-- Sort band: base 27400, step 3 -> threads at 27400, 27403, 27406, 27409 (4 threads)
-- Source of EVERY row: 'canon','isaiah',57,v
--
-- Isaiah 57 coverage:
--   ★ v.1-2 (The righteous perisheth, and no man layeth it to heart... the righteous is taken away from
--          the evil to come. He shall enter into peace: they shall rest in their beds)
--        NT:     ★ Revelation 14:13 (Blessed are the dead which die in Yahuah (Lord)... they may rest
--                from their labours) — THREAD 1
--        Extras: none warranted (the gathered-to-rest weave is carried canon-to-canon)
--        Tanakh: ★ Psalm 12:1 (the godly man ceaseth), Micah 7:2 (the good man is perished out of the
--                earth), 2 Kings 22:20 (Josiah gathered to the grave in peace before the evil — lateral) — THREAD 1
--   v.3-13 (the lawsuit against the sons of the sorceress / the idolaters)
--        NT:     none warranted (covenant-lawsuit on conduct; woven in prose, not forced to a member)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: woven in prose — the contrast that frames the righteous of v.1-2 and the contrite of v.15
--   v.14 (Cast ye up, cast ye up, prepare the way, take up the stumblingblock out of the way of my people)
--        NT:     none warranted distinct (the way-preparing motif held in THREAD 2/3 prose)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: held in prose (the highway for the people who are healed and brought near)
--   ★★ v.15 (the high and lofty One that inhabiteth eternity, whose name is Holy; I dwell in the high
--          and holy place, with him also that is of a contrite and humble spirit)
--        NT:     ★★ Matthew 5:3 (Blessed are the poor in spirit), Matthew 5:4 (Blessed are they that
--                mourn) — THREAD 2
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★★ Isaiah 66:1-2 (heaven my throne... to this man will I look, even to him that is poor
--                and of a contrite spirit), ★ Psalm 34:18 (Yahuah is nigh unto them that are of a broken
--                heart), ★ Psalm 51:17 (a broken and a contrite heart, O Elohim, thou wilt not despise) — THREAD 2
--   v.16-18 (I will not contend for ever... I have seen his ways, and will heal him... and restore comforts)
--        NT:     none warranted distinct (the healing/restoring weave is gathered into THREAD 3's peace)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: held in prose — the preface to the create-the-fruit-of-the-lips peace of v.19
--   ★★★ v.19 (I create the fruit of the lips; Peace, peace to him that is far off, and to him that is
--          near, saith Yahuah; and I will heal him)
--        NT:     ★★★ Ephesians 2:13 (ye who sometimes were far off are made nigh by the blood of
--                Messiah), ★★ Ephesians 2:17 (came and preached peace to you which were afar off, and to
--                them that were nigh), ★ Acts 2:39 (the promise is unto you... and to all that are afar
--                off — lateral) — THREAD 3
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: the far-and-near = the two houses both made nigh, woven in prose (Rom 11:1-2 guard)
--   ★ v.20-21 (the wicked are like the troubled sea... There is no peace, saith my Elohim, to the wicked)
--        NT:     ★ Romans 3:17 (the way of peace have they not known — lateral) — THREAD 4
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★ Isaiah 48:22 (There is no peace, saith Yahuah, unto the wicked — the twin refrain) — THREAD 4
--
-- Threads (slug — target libraries):
--   1. isaiah-57-the-righteous-gathered-to-rest-before-the-evil — NT (Revelation 14) + Tanakh (Psalm 12,
--      Micah 7, 2 Kings 22) [free]
--      (★ the righteous taken away from the evil to come; gathered to rest before the judgment)
--   2. isaiah-57-the-high-and-lofty-one-who-dwells-with-the-contrite — NT (Matthew 5) + Tanakh (Isaiah 66,
--      Psalm 34, Psalm 51) [free]
--      (★★ the transcendent-yet-near Holy One who revives the heart of the contrite)
--   3. isaiah-57-peace-peace-to-him-that-is-far-off-and-to-him-that-is-near — NT (Ephesians 2, Acts 2) [free]
--      (★★★ peace to far and near = the two houses both made nigh; NOT replacement, Rom 11:1-2 guard)
--   4. isaiah-57-there-is-no-peace-to-the-wicked — NT (Romans 3) + Tanakh (Isaiah 48) [free]
--      (★ the twin refrain; the wicked excluded from the peace of v.19)
--
-- Framing notes:
--   ★ THE RIGHTEOUS GATHERED (THREAD 1): *The righteous perisheth, and no man layeth it to heart: and
--      merciful men are taken away, none considering that the righteous is taken away from the evil to
--      come* (57:1); *He shall enter into peace: they shall rest in their beds* (57:2). This is mercy, not
--      loss — the righteous gathered to rest BEFORE the judgment. Revelation seals the blessing: *Blessed
--      are the dead which die in Yahuah (Lord)... that they may rest from their labours* (14:13). The
--      Psalmist and Micah lament the same vanishing of the good (*the godly man ceaseth*, Ps 12:1; *the
--      good man is perished out of the earth*, Micah 7:2), and Josiah is the lateral type — gathered to
--      his grave in peace so his eyes should not see the evil to come (2 Kings 22:20).
--   ★★ THE HIGH AND LOFTY ONE (THREAD 2): *thus saith the high and lofty One that inhabiteth eternity,
--      whose name is Holy; I dwell in the high and holy place, with him also that is of a contrite and
--      humble spirit* (57:15). The Holy One is transcendent AND near — He inhabits eternity and dwells
--      with the broken. Isaiah's own closing word repeats it (*to this man will I look, even to him that
--      is poor and of a contrite spirit*, 66:2); the Psalms sing it (*Yahuah is nigh unto them that are
--      of a broken heart*, 34:18; *a broken and a contrite heart... thou wilt not despise*, 51:17); and
--      Yahusha opens the kingdom to the same (*Blessed are the poor in spirit... Blessed are they that
--      mourn*, Matthew 5:3-4). Framed STRICT Formed/Formless: the high and lofty One whose Name is Holy
--      is the Most High; never trinitarian co-equal grammar, never modalist.
--   ★★★ PEACE FAR AND NEAR (THREAD 3): *I create the fruit of the lips; Peace, peace to him that is far
--      off, and to him that is near, saith Yahuah (LORD); and I will heal him* (57:19). The far and the
--      near are reconciled into one peace — the two-house gospel. Paul names it: *ye who sometimes were
--      far off are made nigh by the blood of Messiah* (Ephesians 2:13); *came and preached peace to you
--      which were afar off, and to them that were nigh* (2:17); and Peter at Pentecost (*the promise is
--      unto you... and to all that are afar off*, Acts 2:39). The scattered of both houses (the far) and
--      those near brought into ONE peace — NEVER replacement, both olive branches Yashar'el (Romans
--      11:1-2 guard).
--   ★ NO PEACE TO THE WICKED (THREAD 4): *There is no peace, saith my Elohim (God), to the wicked* (57:21)
--      — the twin of *There is no peace, saith Yahuah (LORD), unto the wicked* (Isaiah 48:22). The wicked,
--      like *the troubled sea, when it cannot rest* (57:20), are shut out from the peace of v.19. Paul's
--      catena names the same exclusion: *the way of peace have they not known* (Romans 3:17 — lateral).
--   VERSES WITH NO SEPARATE ADD: v.3-13 (the lawsuit against the idolaters — covenant-lawsuit on conduct,
--      the contrast that frames the righteous and the contrite), v.14 (the highway prepared), v.16-18 (I
--      will heal him and restore comforts — the preface to the peace of v.19). All recorded, none silently
--      skipped.

CREATE TEMP VIEW _s303_isa57_lookup AS
SELECT e.slug AS edition_slug, b.slug AS book_slug, c.chapter_number, v.verse_number, v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id=c.id JOIN books b ON c.book_id=b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id=e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN ('canon','enoch','jubilees','jasher','apocrypha','apocrypha-charles-vol1','pseudepigrapha','adam-eve-conflict','apocalypse-of-abraham','ascension-isaiah','sonnini-acts-29');

INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, i.tier::content_tier
  FROM (VALUES
    -- THREAD 1 (★): The righteous gathered to rest before the evil to come
    ('canon','isaiah',57,1,'canon','revelation',14,13,'free',
      E'*And I heard a voice from heaven saying unto me, Write, Blessed are the dead which die in Yahuah (Lord) from henceforth: Yea, saith the Spirit, that they may rest from their labours; and their works do follow them* (Revelation 14:13). This seals the mercy of *the righteous is taken away from the evil to come* (Isaiah 57:1): the gathering of the righteous is not loss but blessing — *Blessed are the dead which die in Yahuah (Lord)... that they may rest from their labours*. They are taken to rest before the judgment, exactly as Isaiah says they *shall rest in their beds* (57:2).'),
    ('canon','isaiah',57,1,'canon','psalms',12,1,'free',
      E'*Help, Yahuah (LORD); for the godly man ceaseth; for the faithful fail from among the children of men* (Psalm 12:1). The Psalmist laments the very vanishing Isaiah names — *The righteous perisheth, and no man layeth it to heart: and merciful men are taken away* (Isaiah 57:1). When *the godly man ceaseth* and *the faithful fail*, it is the merciful being gathered out; the world does not consider it, but it is the righteous taken from the evil to come.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',57,1,'canon','micah',7,2,'free',
      E'*The good man is perished out of the earth: and there is none upright among men: they all lie in wait for blood* (Micah 7:2). Micah weeps the same loss as Isaiah''s *The righteous perisheth... and merciful men are taken away* (Isaiah 57:1): *the good man is perished out of the earth*. The upright vanish from among a generation that hunts for blood — the righteous removed before the day of visitation falls.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',57,2,'canon','2-kings',22,20,'free',
      E'*Behold therefore, I will gather thee unto thy fathers, and thou shalt be gathered into thy grave in peace; and thine eyes shall not see all the evil which I will bring upon this place* (2 Kings 22:20). Josiah is the very pattern of Isaiah''s word: the righteous king *gathered into thy grave in peace* so that *thine eyes shall not see all the evil* — *the righteous is taken away from the evil to come. He shall enter into peace* (Isaiah 57:1-2). Gathered to rest before the judgment.'),

    -- THREAD 2 (★★): The high and lofty One who dwells with the contrite
    ('canon','isaiah',57,15,'canon','isaiah',66,1,'free',
      E'*Thus saith Yahuah (LORD), The heaven is my throne, and the earth is my footstool: where is the house that ye build unto me? and where is the place of my rest?* (Isaiah 66:1). The same transcendence Isaiah declares — *the high and lofty One that inhabiteth eternity, whose name is Holy; I dwell in the high and holy place* (57:15). Heaven His throne, earth His footstool: no house contains Him, yet He stoops to dwell with the contrite.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',57,15,'canon','isaiah',66,2,'free',
      E'*For all those things hath mine hand made, and all those things have been, saith Yahuah (LORD): but to this man will I look, even to him that is poor and of a contrite spirit, and trembleth at my word* (Isaiah 66:2). This is the twin of 57:15 — the One who *inhabiteth eternity* dwells *with him also that is of a contrite and humble spirit*. The high and lofty One looks not to the temple but *to him that is poor and of a contrite spirit, and trembleth at my word*.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',57,15,'canon','psalms',34,18,'free',
      E'*Yahuah (LORD) is nigh unto them that are of a broken heart; and saveth such as be of a contrite spirit* (Psalm 34:18). The Psalmist sings what Isaiah proclaims: the high and lofty One *dwell(s)... with him also that is of a contrite and humble spirit* (57:15) — *Yahuah is nigh unto them that are of a broken heart*. The transcendent Holy One is near to the broken; He saves *such as be of a contrite spirit*.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',57,15,'canon','psalms',51,17,'free',
      E'*The sacrifices of Elohim (God) are a broken spirit: a broken and a contrite heart, O Elohim (God), thou wilt not despise* (Psalm 51:17). The contrite heart Isaiah says Yahuah dwells with — *to revive the spirit of the humble, and to revive the heart of the contrite ones* (57:15) — is the sacrifice Elohim will not despise: *a broken and a contrite heart, O Elohim, thou wilt not despise*. This is the offering the high and lofty One stoops to receive.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',57,15,'canon','matthew',5,3,'free',
      E'*Blessed are the poor in spirit: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 5:3). Yahusha opens the kingdom to the very ones Isaiah says Yahuah dwells with — *him also that is of a contrite and humble spirit* (57:15). *Blessed are the poor in spirit*: the high and lofty One who inhabiteth eternity gives the kingdom to the humble, reviving the spirit of the contrite.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',57,15,'canon','matthew',5,4,'free',
      E'*Blessed are they that mourn: for they shall be comforted* (Matthew 5:4). The comfort Isaiah promises — *to revive the spirit of the humble, and to revive the heart of the contrite ones* (57:15) — is the blessing Yahusha pronounces: *Blessed are they that mourn: for they shall be comforted*. The Holy One who dwells with the contrite revives and comforts the broken heart.'),

    -- THREAD 3 (★★★): Peace, peace to him that is far off, and to him that is near
    ('canon','isaiah',57,19,'canon','ephesians',2,13,'free',
      E'*But now in HaMashiach Yahusha (Christ Jesus) ye who sometimes were far off are made nigh by the blood of Messiah (Christ)* (Ephesians 2:13). Paul gathers Isaiah''s far-and-near into one body: *Peace, peace to him that is far off, and to him that is near, saith Yahuah (LORD); and I will heal him* (57:19) — *ye who sometimes were far off are made nigh by the blood of Messiah*. The scattered (the far) and those near are reconciled into one peace; both houses of Yashar''el brought home, never a people replaced.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',57,19,'canon','ephesians',2,17,'free',
      E'*And came and preached peace to you which were afar off, and to them that were nigh* (Ephesians 2:17). This is Isaiah 57:19 carried forward almost word for word — *Peace, peace to him that is far off, and to him that is near*. The peace Yahuah creates as the fruit of the lips is preached to the far and the near alike; the two made one, both reconciled into a single peace (Rom 11:1-2 guard — never replacement).'),
    ('canon','isaiah',57,19,'canon','acts',2,39,'free',
      E'*For the promise is unto you, and to your children, and to all that are afar off, even as many as Yahuah Eloheinu (the Lord our God) shall call* (Acts 2:39). At Pentecost the promise reaches Isaiah''s far ones — *Peace, peace to him that is far off, and to him that is near* (57:19) — *the promise is unto you... and to all that are afar off*. The near (those gathered at Jerusalem) and the far (the scattered) are called into the one promise; the far and the near made one.'),

    -- THREAD 4 (★): There is no peace to the wicked (the twin refrain)
    ('canon','isaiah',57,21,'canon','isaiah',48,22,'free',
      E'*There is no peace, saith Yahuah (LORD), unto the wicked* (Isaiah 48:22). This is the twin refrain of 57:21 — *There is no peace, saith my Elohim (God), to the wicked* — the same verdict closing both oracles. The peace, peace given to the far and the near (57:19) is barred to the wicked, who are *like the troubled sea, when it cannot rest* (57:20).'),
    ('canon','isaiah',57,21,'canon','romans',3,17,'free',
      E'*And the way of peace have they not known* (Romans 3:17). Paul''s catena names the exclusion Isaiah pronounces: *There is no peace, saith my Elohim (God), to the wicked* (57:21) — *the way of peace have they not known*. The wicked, restless as the troubled sea, are shut out from the peace Yahuah creates for the contrite and the gathered.')
  ) AS i(src_edition,src_slug,src_ch,src_v,tgt_edition,tgt_slug,tgt_ch,tgt_v,tier,note)
  JOIN _s303_isa57_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug=i.src_edition AND sv.book_slug=i.src_slug AND sv.chapter_number=i.src_ch AND sv.verse_number=i.src_v
  JOIN _s303_isa57_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug=i.tgt_edition AND tv.book_slug=i.tgt_slug AND tv.chapter_number=i.tgt_ch AND tv.verse_number=i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 1 (★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-57-the-righteous-gathered-to-rest-before-the-evil',
       E'The righteous taken away from the evil to come — gathered to rest',
       E'The chapter opens with a mercy the world overlooks: *The righteous perisheth, and no man layeth it to heart: and merciful men are taken away, none considering that the righteous is taken away from the evil to come. He shall enter into peace: they shall rest in their beds, each one walking in his uprightness* (Isaiah 57:1-2). This is not loss but gathering — the righteous removed before the judgment falls, taken to rest. Revelation seals the blessing: *Blessed are the dead which die in Yahuah (Lord) from henceforth: Yea, saith the Spirit, that they may rest from their labours; and their works do follow them* (Revelation 14:13). The Psalmist and Micah weep the same vanishing of the good: *Help, Yahuah (LORD); for the godly man ceaseth; for the faithful fail from among the children of men* (Psalm 12:1); *The good man is perished out of the earth: and there is none upright among men* (Micah 7:2). And Josiah is the very pattern, gathered in peace before the day of wrath: *thou shalt be gathered into thy grave in peace; and thine eyes shall not see all the evil which I will bring upon this place* (2 Kings 22:20). The righteous are taken from the evil to come, that they may rest.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27400
  FROM _s303_isa57_lookup sv, _s303_isa57_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=57 AND sv.verse_number=1
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=57 AND ev.verse_number=2
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 2 (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-57-the-high-and-lofty-one-who-dwells-with-the-contrite',
       E'The high and lofty One whose Name is Holy — who dwells with the contrite',
       E'The crown of the chapter is the Name and the nearness of the Most High: *For thus saith the high and lofty One that inhabiteth eternity, whose name is Holy; I dwell in the high and holy place, with him also that is of a contrite and humble spirit, to revive the spirit of the humble, and to revive the heart of the contrite ones* (Isaiah 57:15). He is transcendent — the high and lofty One who inhabiteth eternity, whose Name is Holy (the Most High, the Formless Source; never collapsed into co-equal persons, never a modalist blur) — and yet He stoops to dwell with the broken. Isaiah''s own closing oracle says it again: *The heaven is my throne, and the earth is my footstool* (66:1), yet *to this man will I look, even to him that is poor and of a contrite spirit, and trembleth at my word* (66:2). The Psalms sing the nearness: *Yahuah (LORD) is nigh unto them that are of a broken heart; and saveth such as be of a contrite spirit* (Psalm 34:18); and the contrite heart is the sacrifice He receives — *a broken and a contrite heart, O Elohim (God), thou wilt not despise* (Psalm 51:17). And Yahusha opens the kingdom to the very same: *Blessed are the poor in spirit: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 5:3); *Blessed are they that mourn: for they shall be comforted* (5:4). The Holy One who inhabits eternity revives the heart of the contrite.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27403
  FROM _s303_isa57_lookup sv, _s303_isa57_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=57 AND sv.verse_number=15
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=57 AND ev.verse_number=15
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 3 (★★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-57-peace-peace-to-him-that-is-far-off-and-to-him-that-is-near',
       E'Peace, peace to him that is far off, and to him that is near — the two houses made one',
       E'Out of the healing of v.18 comes the gospel of the two houses: *I create the fruit of the lips; Peace, peace to him that is far off, and to him that is near, saith Yahuah (LORD); and I will heal him* (Isaiah 57:19). The far and the near are reconciled into ONE peace. Paul reads it straight into the gathering of Yashar''el: *But now in HaMashiach Yahusha (Christ Jesus) ye who sometimes were far off are made nigh by the blood of Messiah (Christ)* (Ephesians 2:13), and he echoes Isaiah almost word for word — *And came and preached peace to you which were afar off, and to them that were nigh* (2:17). At Pentecost the same promise reaches the scattered: *For the promise is unto you, and to your children, and to all that are afar off, even as many as Yahuah Eloheinu (the Lord our God) shall call* (Acts 2:39). The near (those gathered, the house of Yahudah) and the far (the scattered, the divorced house of Yashar''el / Ephraim) are brought into a single peace — both olive branches the same people, regathered and made one. This is NOT a new people replacing Israel; it is the far and the near of the two houses reconciled (Romans 11:1-2 guard — *Hath Elohim (God) cast away his people? Elohim (God) forbid*).',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27406
  FROM _s303_isa57_lookup sv, _s303_isa57_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=57 AND sv.verse_number=19
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=57 AND ev.verse_number=19
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 4 (★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-57-there-is-no-peace-to-the-wicked',
       E'There is no peace, saith my Elohim, to the wicked — the twin refrain',
       E'The chapter closes the door the peace of v.19 opened: *But the wicked are like the troubled sea, when it cannot rest, whose waters cast up mire and dirt. There is no peace, saith my Elohim (God), to the wicked* (Isaiah 57:20-21). This is the twin of the refrain that sealed an earlier oracle — *There is no peace, saith Yahuah (LORD), unto the wicked* (Isaiah 48:22) — the same verdict pronounced twice over the unrepentant. The peace, peace given to the far and the near (57:19) and the rest given to the contrite and the gathered (57:1-2, 15) is barred from the wicked, who can no more rest than the troubled sea. Paul''s catena names the same exclusion: *And the way of peace have they not known* (Romans 3:17). The peace Yahuah creates is for the broken and the healed; the wicked, restless and tossing, are shut out.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27409
  FROM _s303_isa57_lookup sv, _s303_isa57_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=57 AND sv.verse_number=20
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=57 AND ev.verse_number=21
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 1 members (★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_thread_members (thread_id, cross_reference_id, sort_order, member_note)
SELECT t.id, cr.id, 1, E'★ *Blessed are the dead which die in Yahuah (Lord)... that they may rest from their labours* (Revelation 14:13) — the gathering of *the righteous... taken away from the evil to come* (Isaiah 57:1) is blessing, not loss; they enter into rest.'
  FROM cross_reference_threads t
  JOIN _s303_isa57_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=57 AND sv.verse_number=1
  JOIN _s303_isa57_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug='canon' AND tv.book_slug='revelation' AND tv.chapter_number=14 AND tv.verse_number=13
